{"id":130,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"I suspect this Pokémon to be the true identity of a dragon written of in ancient texts, which claimed that it razed an entire village with white-hot beams from its maw."},{"games":["Shield","White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"Once it begins to rampage, a Gyarados will burn everything down, even in a harsh storm."},{"games":["Sword","FireRed"],"text":"It has an extremely aggressive nature. The Hyper Beam it shoots from its mouth totally incinerates all targets."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"Brutally vicious and enormously destructive. Known for totally destroying cities in ancient times."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"The energy from evolution stimulated its brain cells strongly, causing it to become very ferocious."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"It fires hyper beams in all directions, burning the surrounding area to ash. There are some regions where it’s called “the deity of destruction.”"},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"There are people who swear that any place Gyarados appears is fated for destruction."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"A tale is told of a town that angered Gyarados. Before the sun rose the next day, flames utterly consumed the town, leaving not a trace behind."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Once Gyarados goes on a rampage, its ferociously violent blood doesn’t calm until it has burned everything down. There are records of this Pokémon’s rampages lasting a whole month."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"When Magikarp evolves into Gyarados, its brain cells undergo a structural transformation. It is said that this transformation is to blame for this Pokémon’s wildly violent nature."},{"games":["Y","LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"Rarely seen in the wild. Huge and vicious, it is capable of destroying entire cities in a rage."},{"games":["X","Pearl"],"text":"In ancient literature, there is a record of a Gyarados that razed a village when violence flared."},{"games":["SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"Once it appears, it goes on a rampage. It remains enraged until it demolishes everything around it."},{"games":["HeartGold"],"text":"They say that during past strife, GYARADOS would appear and leave blazing ruins in its wake."},{"games":["Diamond"],"text":"Once it appears, its rage never settles until it has razed the fields and mountains around it."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"It is an extremely vicious and violent POKéMON. When humans begin to fight, it will appear and burn everything to the ground with intensely hot flames."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"It appears whenever there is world conflict, burning down any place it travels through."},{"games":["Gold"],"text":"They say that during past wars, GYARADOS would appear and leave blazing ruins in its wake."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Intimidate","hidden":false,"description":"When the Pokémon enters a battle, it intimidates opposing Pokémon and makes them cower, lowering their Attack stats."},{"name":"Moxie","hidden":true,"description":"When the Pokémon knocks out a target, it shows moxie, which boosts its Attack stat."}],"eggGroups":["Water 2","Dragon"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":5,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"slow","habitat":"water's edge","color":"Blue","shape":"Squiggle","evolution":{"id":129,"name":"Magikarp","condition":null,"children":[{"id":130,"name":"Gyarados","condition":"Lv. 20","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[0,44],[1,33],[1,43],[1,150],[1,175],[1,239],[4,250],[8,423],[12,362],[16,184],[21,127],[24,242],[28,240],[32,401],[36,349],[40,56],[44,542],[48,37],[52,63]],"machine":[419,59,34,523,886,242,399,38,913,349,406,525,89,283,203,263,126,53,416,270,542,56,63,58,423,196,442,808,330,200,182,240,156,46,201,503,799,184,214,180,444,164,241,57,36,269,915,851,87,86,85,352,127,250],"egg":[],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"sv10-49","name":"Misty's Gyarados","set":"Destined Rivals","date":"2025-05-30",